# Electron Main Process Instructions

## Directory Structure

```
electron/
├── main.ts                      → Entry point: loads AppBootstrap with app entities & services
├── preload.ts                   → Re-exports framework preload (contextBridge)
├── tsconfig.json                → TypeScript config (commonjs, es2020)
├── dist-electron/               → Compiled output (generated by tsc)
└── src/
    ├── controllers/
    │   ├── index.ts             → CONTROLLERS array (side-effect imports)
    │   └── ...                  → App-specific IPC controllers
    ├── services/
    │   ├── index.ts             → Exports APP_SERVICES array
    │   └── ...                  → App-specific business logic services
    └── db/
        └── entities/
            └── index.ts         → MODELS array (TypeORM entities)
```

**Framework provides** (imported from `{{PKG}}/electron`):
- `AppBootstrap` — main bootstrap orchestrator
- `Injectable`, `Injector` — mini-pie DI system
- `Controller`, `IpcHandler` — IPC decorators
- `PushChannel`, `PushEvent`, `PushEmitter` — push event system
- `BaseController` — controller base class with `success()`/`error()`
- `Logger` — Electron logging
- All system services: `ConfigService`, `DataSourceService`, `AppConfigService`, `BackupService`, `UpdaterService`, etc.
- `initChronomancerForElectron`, `Chronomancer` — performance tracking

## Bootstrap Flow

```
electron/main.ts
  → app.whenReady()
  → AppBootstrap.init({ models: MODELS, services: [...SYSTEM_SERVICES, ...APP_SERVICES], controllers: CONTROLLERS })
    → Injector.load(SERVICES) — topologically sorted DI
    → AppBootstrapService.bootstrap()
      → Init Chronomancer (performance tracking)
      → Load app config from package.json
      → Initialize DataSource (TypeORM + SQLite)
      → Register all controllers (IPC handlers)
      → Create splash window (if enabled)
      → Create main window
      → Init context menu
      → Run startup tasks (backup, updates)
      → Print performance report
```

### main.ts Pattern

```typescript
import { AppBootstrap } from '{{PKG}}/electron';
import { MODELS } from './src/db/entities';
import { APP_SERVICES } from './src/services';
import './src/controllers'; // side-effect: registers controllers

AppBootstrap.init({
  models: MODELS,
  services: [...APP_SERVICES],
});
```

### preload.ts

```typescript
import '{{PKG}}/preload';
```

## mini-pie DI System

Custom lightweight dependency injection in the framework.

- `@Injectable()` decorator marks a class for DI (no parameters)
- `Injector.load(classes)` performs topological sort and instantiates singletons
- `Injector.inject(Class)` retrieves the singleton instance
- Dependencies resolved via constructor parameter types using `reflect-metadata`
- Requires `emitDecoratorMetadata: true` in tsconfig
- Circular dependencies are detected and throw errors

## Controller Pattern

Controllers handle IPC requests from Angular renderer.

```typescript
import { Controller, IpcHandler, BaseController } from '{{PKG}}/electron';

@Controller({ prefix: "myPrefix" })
export class MyController extends BaseController {
  constructor(private readonly myService: MyService) { super(); }

  @IpcHandler("action")
  async handleAction(arg1: string, arg2: number) {
    try {
      const result = await this.myService.doSomething(arg1, arg2);
      return this.success(result);
    } catch (error) {
      return this.error(error);
    }
  }

  @IpcHandler("list")
  async getList() {
    try {
      const items = await this.myService.getAll();
      return this.success(items);
    } catch (error) {
      return this.error(error);
    }
  }
}
```

Rules:
- Always extend `BaseController`
- Use `this.success(data)` and `this.error(error)` — never return raw objects
- Full IPC channel: `{prefix}:{handlerName}` (e.g. `myPrefix:action`)
- Every handler should try/catch and return error via `this.error()`
- Register in `CONTROLLERS` array in `electron/src/controllers/index.ts` (side-effect import)

### controllers/index.ts Pattern

```typescript
import './my.controller';
import './other.controller';
// Controllers are auto-registered via @Controller decorator side-effects
```

## Service Pattern

Services contain business logic and are auto-injected.

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '{{PKG}}/electron';

@Injectable()
export class MyService {
  constructor(
    private readonly configService: ConfigService,
    private readonly dataSourceService: DataSourceService
  ) {}

  async getAll(): Promise<MyEntity[]> {
    const repo = this.dataSourceService.model(MyEntity);
    return repo.find();
  }

  async save(data: Partial<MyEntity>): Promise<MyEntity> {
    const repo = this.dataSourceService.model(MyEntity);
    return repo.save(data);
  }

  async delete(id: number): Promise<void> {
    const repo = this.dataSourceService.model(MyEntity);
    await repo.delete(id);
  }
}
```

Rules:
- Always `@Injectable()` with no parameters
- Constructor injection only (type-based resolution)
- Register in `APP_SERVICES` array in `electron/src/services/index.ts`
- Services are singletons — one instance for entire app lifetime
- Load order determined automatically by topological sort of dependency graph

### services/index.ts Pattern

```typescript
import { MyService } from './my.service';

export { MyService };

export const APP_SERVICES = [MyService];
```

## Push Events Pattern (Main → Renderer)

For sending real-time events from Electron to Angular.

```typescript
import { Injectable, PushChannel, PushEvent, PushEmitter } from '{{PKG}}/electron';

@PushChannel('myChannel')
@Injectable()
export class MyService {
  @PushEvent('data-changed')
  dataEmitter = new PushEmitter<MyData>();

  @PushEvent('progress')
  progressEmitter = new PushEmitter<number>();

  async updateData() {
    this.progressEmitter.emit(0);
    const data = await this.fetchData();
    this.dataEmitter.emit(data);
    this.progressEmitter.emit(100);
  }
}
```

- `@PushChannel(prefix)` on class level — defines channel group
- `@PushEvent(name)` on property level — defines event name
- Property must be typed `PushEmitter<T>`
- Full channel: `push:{prefix}:{eventName}` (e.g. `push:myChannel:data-changed`)
- PushService automatically initializes emitters via metadata reflection
- Angular subscribes via `ElectronPushService.on<T>('push:myChannel:data-changed')`

## TypeORM Entities

```typescript
import { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, CreateDateColumn, ManyToOne } from 'typeorm';

@Entity()
export class MyEntity {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
  id!: number;

  @Column()
  name!: string;

  @Column({ nullable: true })
  description?: string;

  @Column({ default: true })
  active!: boolean;

  @CreateDateColumn()
  createdAt!: Date;
}
```

- Register in `MODELS` array in `electron/src/db/entities/index.ts`
- Access via `this.dataSourceService.model(MyEntity)` → returns TypeORM Repository
- `synchronize: true` — schema updates automatically
- Supports all TypeORM decorators: `@Column`, `@ManyToOne`, `@OneToMany`, `@ManyToMany`, `@Index`, etc.

### entities/index.ts Pattern

```typescript
import { MyEntity } from './my-entity';

export { MyEntity };

export const MODELS = [MyEntity];
```

## Framework System Services Reference

These services are provided by the framework. Import from `{{PKG}}/electron`:

| Service | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `AppConfigService` | App info from package.json + persistent settings |
| `DataSourceService` | TypeORM DataSource init + `.model(Entity)` for repositories |
| `ControllerService` | Registers controllers' IPC handlers on ipcMain |
| `PushService` | Initializes PushEmitters, sends events to renderer |
| `BackupService` | DB backup/restore (auto + manual), integrity check |
| `UpdaterService` | Check/download/install updates, status push events |
| `ConfigService` | Persistent JSON config file read/write |
| `DbConfigService` | Database file path configuration |
| `AppDataService` | App data directory paths |
| `DevModeService` | Development mode detection (`ELECTRON_IS_DEV` env) |
| `LifecycleService` | App quit/window close handlers |
| `CacheService` | In-memory caching |
| `ElectronMainWindowService` | Main BrowserWindow creation |
| `ElectronSplashWindowService` | Splash screen window |
| `ElectronWindowService` | Window management utilities |
| `ContextMenuService` | Right-click context menu |
| `NotificationService` | Notification system (Electron side) |
| `ErrorNotificationService` | Error notification handling |

## IpcResponse Type

All controller methods must return this shape:
```typescript
interface IpcResponse<T = unknown> {
  success: boolean;
  data?: T;
  error?: string;
}
```

`BaseController.success(data)` and `BaseController.error(error)` produce this automatically.

## Database Path Logic

- **Development**: `app.getAppPath()/database/`
- **Installed**: `app.getPath('userData')/database/`
- **Portable**: `path.dirname(app.getPath('exe'))/database/` (detected via marker file)

## TypeScript Configuration

`electron/tsconfig.json`:
- `"module": "commonjs"`, `"target": "es2020"`
- `"experimentalDecorators": true`, `"emitDecoratorMetadata": true` (required for mini-pie DI)
- `"strictPropertyInitialization": false` (for DI injected properties)
- Outputs to `electron/dist-electron/`

## Code Generation

Use VS Code tasks or CLI to generate Electron elements:
```bash
npx eaf generate electron-service <name>      # Creates service + updates index.ts
npx eaf generate electron-controller <name>   # Creates controller + updates index.ts
```

## Complete Example: Adding a New Feature

Here's a complete walkthrough of adding a "Todo" feature end-to-end:

### 1. Create Entity (`electron/src/db/entities/todo.ts`)

```typescript
import { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, CreateDateColumn } from 'typeorm';

@Entity()
export class Todo {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
  id!: number;

  @Column()
  title!: string;

  @Column({ default: false })
  completed!: boolean;

  @CreateDateColumn()
  createdAt!: Date;
}
```

Register in `electron/src/db/entities/index.ts`:
```typescript
import { Todo } from './todo';
export { Todo };
export const MODELS = [Todo];
```

### 2. Create Service (`electron/src/services/todo.service.ts`)

```typescript
import { Injectable, DataSourceService } from '{{PKG}}/electron';
import { Todo } from '../db/entities/todo';

@Injectable()
export class TodoService {
  constructor(private readonly dataSourceService: DataSourceService) {}

  async getAll(): Promise<Todo[]> {
    return this.dataSourceService.model(Todo).find({ order: { createdAt: 'DESC' } });
  }

  async create(title: string): Promise<Todo> {
    return this.dataSourceService.model(Todo).save({ title });
  }

  async toggle(id: number): Promise<Todo | null> {
    const repo = this.dataSourceService.model(Todo);
    const todo = await repo.findOneBy({ id });
    if (!todo) return null;
    todo.completed = !todo.completed;
    return repo.save(todo);
  }

  async delete(id: number): Promise<void> {
    await this.dataSourceService.model(Todo).delete(id);
  }
}
```

Register in `electron/src/services/index.ts`:
```typescript
import { TodoService } from './todo.service';
export { TodoService };
export const APP_SERVICES = [TodoService];
```

### 3. Create Controller (`electron/src/controllers/todo.controller.ts`)

```typescript
import { Controller, IpcHandler, BaseController } from '{{PKG}}/electron';
import { TodoService } from '../services/todo.service';

@Controller({ prefix: 'todo' })
export class TodoController extends BaseController {
  constructor(private readonly todoService: TodoService) { super(); }

  @IpcHandler('list')
  async list() {
    try {
      const todos = await this.todoService.getAll();
      return this.success(todos);
    } catch (error) {
      return this.error(error);
    }
  }

  @IpcHandler('create')
  async create(title: string) {
    try {
      const todo = await this.todoService.create(title);
      return this.success(todo);
    } catch (error) {
      return this.error(error);
    }
  }

  @IpcHandler('toggle')
  async toggle(id: number) {
    try {
      const todo = await this.todoService.toggle(id);
      return this.success(todo);
    } catch (error) {
      return this.error(error);
    }
  }

  @IpcHandler('delete')
  async remove(id: number) {
    try {
      await this.todoService.delete(id);
      return this.success(null);
    } catch (error) {
      return this.error(error);
    }
  }
}
```

Register in `electron/src/controllers/index.ts`:
```typescript
import './todo.controller';
```

### 4. IPC Channels Created

| Channel | Handler | Description |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| `todo:list` | `list()` | Get all todos |
| `todo:create` | `create(title)` | Create a new todo |
| `todo:toggle` | `toggle(id)` | Toggle todo completion |
| `todo:delete` | `remove(id)` | Delete a todo |

These channels are called from Angular via `window.electronAPI.invoke('todo:list')`, etc.
